\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. As pants the hart for cooling streams,
\par When heated in the chase,
\par So longs my soul, O God, for Thee,
\par And Thy refreshing grace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. For Thee, my God, the living God,
\par My thirsty soul doth pine;
\par O when shall I behold Thy face,
\par Thou Majesty divine!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. God of my strength, how long shall I,
\par Like one forgotten, mourn?
\par Forlorn, forsaken, and exposed
\par To my oppressor's scorn.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Why restless, why cast down, my soul?
\par Hope still, and thou shalt sing
\par The praise of Him who is thy God,
\par Thy health's eternal spring.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

